---
description: Schema and versioning conventions for Trustilo's core data model (Question, Evidence, Answer, Citation, VerificationResult, ReviewTask, AuditEvent). Applies when adding fields, creating new schemas, or touching src/trustilo/common/schemas.py or specs/02-data-model.md.
alwaysApply: false
---
- Use the canonical Pydantic models in `src/trustilo/common/schemas.py`
  for every cross-stage payload. Don't pass ad hoc dicts between
  stages — if a stage needs a new field, add it to the schema.
- `EvidenceChunk` is invalid without `doc_id`, `version`, `source`, and
  `tenant_id` — this is a hard validator, not a code-review reminder
  (FR3's literal success criterion).
- A `Claim` with zero citations is only valid when the parent
  `Answer.abstained is True`. Enforce this as a model validator.
- `EscalationDecision.reason_codes` must be non-empty whenever
  `decision == "escalate"` (NFR9).
- IDs are opaque strings (e.g. ULIDs) generated client-side, not
  auto-increment integers — this is what makes idempotent retries in
  the Orchestrator possible.
- Superseding a document's version never deletes old `EvidenceChunk`
  rows — mark them superseded so existing citations still resolve.
- Any schema change: update `specs/02-data-model.md`'s table in the
  same commit. The two must never drift.
